[Cheonji Ilbo Chungbuk=Reporter Kim Heung-soon] Chungbuk is facing a real crisis as youth outmigration and market stagnation continue despite population growth. Last year, 6800 young people left, and vacancy rates in downtown areas like Seongan-gil have risen.

Young people are leaving due to a lack of jobs, culture, and housing opportunities. Experts emphasize, &ldquo;Strengthening settlement infrastructure and integrating universities are essential.&rdquo;

The province plans to invest 404.1 billion KRW by 2025 across 99 youth policies. Yet many young people say, &ldquo;There are many policies, but we don&rsquo;t feel their impact.&rdquo;

A spokesperson for the provincial government responded, &ldquo;We are enhancing both online and localized promotion to increase the perceived impact of youth policies.&rdquo;
